1
00:00:10,135 --> 00:00:12,512
Oh, Congressman Romero,

2
00:00:12,513 --> 00:00:16,057
I just wanted to see you one last time
before I leave.

3
00:00:16,058 --> 00:00:17,726
I don't believe
there's anything left to be said.

4
00:00:17,727 --> 00:00:20,478
No, not between us. Not any longer.

5
00:00:20,479 --> 00:00:25,859
I just wanted to thank you for...
your tenacity.

6
00:00:27,903 --> 00:00:30,238
Whatever you're up to,
you won't get away with it.

7
00:00:30,239 --> 00:00:32,240
Maybe I already have.

8
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:36,745
The committee will continue its work.
We'll recommend charges to DOJ.

9
00:00:37,913 --> 00:00:39,331
Rochelle.

10
00:00:50,217 --> 00:00:51,760
Rochelle.

11
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:54,930
Such a lovely name.

12
00:00:56,557 --> 00:00:59,810
Tell me how much you don't want that
to end up in the press.

13
00:01:00,853 --> 00:01:03,563
And then shut this committee down.

14
00:01:03,564 --> 00:01:04,898
No deals.

15
00:01:09,527 --> 00:01:12,114
Mr. President! Mr. President!

16
00:03:00,555 --> 00:03:01,848
How could you?

17
00:03:01,849 --> 00:03:04,225
- How could you not warn me?
- To protect you.

18
00:03:04,226 --> 00:03:06,895
- I was protecting you.
- You should take your hands off me.

19
00:03:06,896 --> 00:03:08,855
No, look, I understand
if you feel broadsided.

20
00:03:08,856 --> 00:03:10,899
- I don't care about feelings, Francis.
- But listen to me...

21
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:13,734
- Look, Claire, listen to me.
- You made me look absolutely ridiculous.

22
00:03:13,735 --> 00:03:15,695
- Ill-prepared and ignorant.
- No! Claire.

23
00:03:15,696 --> 00:03:18,197
- We have one rule, Francis. One rule.
- No, not anymore.

24
00:03:18,198 --> 00:03:19,699
Not anymore. We don't.

25
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:22,618
I cannot be your ally
if I don't know what you're thinking.

26
00:03:22,619 --> 00:03:24,996
Listen, Claire. It would have never ended.

27
00:03:24,997 --> 00:03:27,581
All right, fine, we got to stop judiciary,

28
00:03:27,582 --> 00:03:31,252
but other committees would have sprung up,
just to keep the charges going.

29
00:03:31,253 --> 00:03:34,839
Oversight, Armed Services,
Foreign Affairs, Intelligence.

30
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,007
It would have gone on and on.

31
00:03:36,008 --> 00:03:37,759
- Years and years of investigation.
- I don't care.

32
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:39,302
You should have talked to me,

33
00:03:39,303 --> 00:03:41,763
instead of making
a last-minute decision like this.

34
00:03:41,764 --> 00:03:42,890
I didn't.

35
00:03:44,557 --> 00:03:50,230
I created this confusion
in order to take advantage of it.

36
00:03:50,814 --> 00:03:55,527
Everything that has happened...
was planned.

37
00:03:57,946 --> 00:03:59,613
Since when?

38
00:03:59,614 --> 00:04:01,992
Since before Elysian Fields.

39
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:05,411
But it was at Elysian Fields
that it hit me.

40
00:04:05,412 --> 00:04:11,293
I saw it... almost like a light bulb
going off above my head.

41
00:04:12,710 --> 00:04:15,755
Where does the real power lie?

42
00:04:15,756 --> 00:04:19,134
The power behind the power.

43
00:04:20,218 --> 00:04:21,845
And I understood, Claire,

44
00:04:21,846 --> 00:04:26,474
that we have to think and act differently
than we ever have.

45
00:04:26,475 --> 00:04:30,020
Because it's no longer about
who lives in the White House...

46
00:04:32,439 --> 00:04:35,691
it's about who owns the White House.

47
00:04:35,692 --> 00:04:39,320
This is the presidency.
How much higher can a politician go?

48
00:04:39,321 --> 00:04:41,782
The real power isn't here.

49
00:04:43,075 --> 00:04:44,700
It's beyond here.

50
00:04:44,701 --> 00:04:47,996
It's above it, but still working
in conjunction with it.

51
00:04:47,997 --> 00:04:50,832
Look, Claire,
you and I have always been on the inside.

52
00:04:50,833 --> 00:04:53,501
Trapped. In the bubble.

53
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:56,588
But going forward...

54
00:04:57,547 --> 00:05:01,342
with my operating on the outside,
in the private sector,

55
00:05:01,343 --> 00:05:04,554
and you working from here...

56
00:05:06,764 --> 00:05:09,935
we can own this house together.

57
00:05:12,645 --> 00:05:16,649
Don't you see? I've designed this.

58
00:05:17,818 --> 00:05:20,403
I wanted you to be the president.

59
00:05:21,071 --> 00:05:24,616
I've made you the president.

60
00:05:27,828 --> 00:05:29,787
Am I supposed to say thank you?

61
00:05:30,455 --> 00:05:31,998
No.

62
00:05:31,999 --> 00:05:36,252
But you will have to pardon me.
Pardon me for all of my crimes.

63
00:05:36,253 --> 00:05:38,421
As the president,
you're the only one who can.

64
00:05:38,422 --> 00:05:40,256
Francis, I could be impeached
if I do that.

65
00:05:40,257 --> 00:05:44,052
No, no. Look, Davis and Usher,
they're in a position to protect you.

66
00:05:44,053 --> 00:05:47,221
- They want you to succeed.
- We can be sure of nothing, Francis.

67
00:05:47,222 --> 00:05:49,933
Everything going on with Doug,
the leak still in the White House...

68
00:05:49,934 --> 00:05:51,768
No, that was me, too.

69
00:05:53,686 --> 00:05:55,605
- What?
- I'm the leak.

70
00:05:56,564 --> 00:05:58,566
I've been feeding information
to Tom Hammerschmidt

71
00:05:58,567 --> 00:06:00,485
for months with Doug's help.

72
00:06:02,237 --> 00:06:04,905
That doesn't make any sense, Francis.

73
00:06:04,906 --> 00:06:07,616
Claire, when you bring yourself down
before someone else can,

74
00:06:07,617 --> 00:06:09,661
you control the way it happens.

75
00:06:10,787 --> 00:06:15,916
This was the only path
to get us to this moment

76
00:06:15,917 --> 00:06:19,837
where you and I can own it all.

77
00:06:28,388 --> 00:06:30,640
Get rid of the surveillance.

78
00:06:31,308 --> 00:06:35,353
Erase it. Shut everything down.
Anything you and Doug were up to.

79
00:06:35,354 --> 00:06:38,689
All right.
But you have to pardon me first.

80
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:43,153
And, at the right time, Doug.
Or we could both go to prison.

81
00:06:46,406 --> 00:06:48,241
I killed Tom.

82
00:06:48,242 --> 00:06:50,785
I killed Tom Yates. He's dead.

83
00:06:52,204 --> 00:06:54,289
And I had Mark clean it up.

84
00:06:55,748 --> 00:06:58,710
So it will never make its way back to us.

85
00:07:04,466 --> 00:07:06,969
Well, then I guess we both did
what we had to.

86
00:07:09,346 --> 00:07:11,055
- Did you know he was gonna do this?
- No.

87
00:07:11,056 --> 00:07:15,352
- Because this is bad, Claire.
- This is very... very bad.

88
00:07:17,604 --> 00:07:19,064
My God!

89
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:21,857
What is it with you two?

90
00:07:21,858 --> 00:07:25,069
- If there's something on your mind, say...
- In my house?

91
00:07:25,070 --> 00:07:26,445
You left him in my house?!

92
00:07:26,446 --> 00:07:29,699
Lower your voice,
or at least change your tone.

93
00:07:30,492 --> 00:07:32,035
Did you take care of it?

94
00:07:34,621 --> 00:07:36,455
Yes, that's what I do.

95
00:07:36,456 --> 00:07:38,291
Then thank you, and well done.

96
00:07:39,126 --> 00:07:40,751
Now let's get back
to what's in front of us.

97
00:07:40,752 --> 00:07:42,753
Does he even want you to be here, Claire?

98
00:07:42,754 --> 00:07:45,381
Mark, please. What I need right now
is your political calculus.

99
00:07:45,382 --> 00:07:49,177
He has put you, he has put all of us,
in an impossible position.

100
00:07:49,178 --> 00:07:50,553
You see that?

101
00:07:52,055 --> 00:07:55,308
If you don't handle this correctly,
you do not recover from it.

102
00:07:55,309 --> 00:07:58,311
This is about continuity of government.

103
00:07:59,312 --> 00:08:03,899
Informing NATO, informing world leaders.
We should have had ambassadors on call.

104
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:05,985
Joint Chiefs of Staff,
the National Security...

105
00:08:05,986 --> 00:08:08,405
Even Nixon did that!

106
00:08:12,575 --> 00:08:14,368
<i>I'm ready to hand it over,</i>

107
00:08:14,369 --> 00:08:16,079
<i>but I want to be assured
that no matter what,</i>

108
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:18,122
<i>Macallan's death is not related to me.</i>

109
00:08:18,123 --> 00:08:20,124
That can be taken care of.

110
00:08:20,125 --> 00:08:22,752
- I want what you have of mine.
<i>- Okay.</i>

111
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:24,670
That's what you'll get.

112
00:08:24,671 --> 00:08:27,049
And I want to be Chief of Staff.

113
00:08:29,426 --> 00:08:31,511
Well, I don't think that's a problem.

114
00:08:32,345 --> 00:08:34,597
I'm glad you're asking for what you want.

115
00:08:41,104 --> 00:08:43,564
Doug Stamper would do anything
for the president.

116
00:08:43,565 --> 00:08:46,943
He saw a threat in Zoe Barnes,
who the president was involved with.

117
00:08:47,610 --> 00:08:49,362
And he took care of it.

118
00:08:49,363 --> 00:08:51,698
He's threatened my life
on numerous occasions.

119
00:08:52,865 --> 00:08:55,409
- But to go back to my question...
- No, ma'am.

120
00:08:55,410 --> 00:08:58,454
I don't think the president knew
what Doug was up to.

121
00:08:58,455 --> 00:08:59,872
Not at all.

122
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:07,964
Mr. Hammerschmidt.

123
00:09:08,881 --> 00:09:10,467
I've been meaning to call you.

124
00:09:14,096 --> 00:09:15,180
Sean.

125
00:09:16,223 --> 00:09:17,932
As you can tell, I work here now.

126
00:09:19,642 --> 00:09:24,063
I'm shaking your hand right now
because I believe in social graces.

127
00:09:26,524 --> 00:09:27,692
You're lost.

128
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:31,779
- I don't think so.
- No, you are.

129
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:33,697
No, not at all.

130
00:09:33,698 --> 00:09:35,200
This is what you wanted?

131
00:09:35,825 --> 00:09:40,579
A job in a corrupt administration?
Presidency in ruin?

132
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:43,583
I'm in the White House. Not out there,
wondering what it's like in here.

133
00:09:45,460 --> 00:09:48,045
Not for long.

134
00:09:48,046 --> 00:09:51,757
Once you're in, you're in.
It's the American way.

135
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:54,594
- Mr. Stamper will see you now.
- Thank you.

136
00:10:02,269 --> 00:10:04,019
Sorry to keep you waiting.

137
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:05,438
When I asked for this meeting,
I had no idea

138
00:10:05,439 --> 00:10:08,441
the president would be signing
his resignation this evening.

139
00:10:09,359 --> 00:10:11,694
And I, this morning.

140
00:10:12,279 --> 00:10:14,947
- I heard a rumor you might.
- Now it's confirmed.

141
00:10:14,948 --> 00:10:16,324
Mr. Stamper...

142
00:10:16,325 --> 00:10:18,785
Yeah, please. You can call me Doug.

143
00:10:19,536 --> 00:10:22,913
I'd rather not,
for the sake of this interview.

144
00:10:22,914 --> 00:10:25,208
I want you to know
this will not be off the record,

145
00:10:25,209 --> 00:10:26,501
or on background.

146
00:10:29,212 --> 00:10:32,924
I do know Lisa Williams.
I met her a couple years ago.

147
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:36,928
Okay.

148
00:10:37,845 --> 00:10:39,972
But before we get to anything else...

149
00:10:42,392 --> 00:10:46,229
did President Underwood,
when he was congressman, kill Zoe Barnes?

150
00:10:49,566 --> 00:10:50,817
No.

151
00:10:51,693 --> 00:10:52,610
Mr. Stamper...

152
00:10:56,656 --> 00:10:58,824
did you kill Zoe Barnes?

153
00:10:58,825 --> 00:11:01,077
I'm not prepared to answer that question.

154
00:11:02,119 --> 00:11:05,122
You understand I can use
your refusal in print.

155
00:11:05,957 --> 00:11:07,500
Yes.

156
00:11:07,501 --> 00:11:10,336
Were you on the Cathedral Heights
D.C. Metro platform

157
00:11:10,337 --> 00:11:11,712
the day of Zoe's death?

158
00:11:11,713 --> 00:11:15,633
Any questions regarding Zoe Barnes,
you need to speak with my attorneys.

159
00:11:20,222 --> 00:11:23,056
Did Zoe Barnes make a call
to Francis Underwood

160
00:11:23,057 --> 00:11:25,768
from a burner phone
when he was congressman?

161
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:29,229
- Why would you ask me that?
- Why won't you answer?

162
00:11:29,230 --> 00:11:31,732
I almost always answer
the president's phone.

163
00:11:31,733 --> 00:11:33,401
Calls, texts...

164
00:11:35,862 --> 00:11:37,655
Do you have any knowledge of those texts?

165
00:11:37,656 --> 00:11:39,699
I'm not prepared to comment on that.

166
00:11:40,492 --> 00:11:42,660
Then this conversation is over.

167
00:11:48,875 --> 00:11:50,293
Have a good day.

168
00:11:55,089 --> 00:11:56,299
One last thing.

169
00:11:57,300 --> 00:11:59,302
Did you send me two birthday cards?

170
00:11:59,969 --> 00:12:00,970
No.

171
00:12:07,810 --> 00:12:09,562
<i>Slàinte mhath.</i>

172
00:12:09,563 --> 00:12:11,855
That's Scottish Gaelic.
It means "good health."

173
00:12:11,856 --> 00:12:13,691
My father's kind of obsessed.

174
00:12:13,692 --> 00:12:17,528
And he traced our line of Graysons
back to, like, 16th century or something.

175
00:12:17,529 --> 00:12:20,948
Hmm. Well, if we ever needed a drink
in the middle of the day...

176
00:12:22,116 --> 00:12:24,994
It went well with the US attorney.

177
00:12:26,871 --> 00:12:28,247
It's tragic.

178
00:12:28,873 --> 00:12:32,377
Our hearts are just broken
at the thought of what Doug did.

179
00:12:33,252 --> 00:12:34,921
I don't know what happened to him.

180
00:12:35,630 --> 00:12:37,924
I guess somewhere along the line...

181
00:12:39,216 --> 00:12:41,385
When will, uh,
he be announcing his resignation?

182
00:12:41,386 --> 00:12:44,847
- It's happening this afternoon.
- Oh, of course.

183
00:12:44,848 --> 00:12:47,266
And, Seth, you'll need to resign as well.

184
00:12:49,936 --> 00:12:53,772
- Uh... Um, I thought that, uh...
- I know, but think about this.

185
00:12:53,773 --> 00:12:57,610
I need to establish my own team. Publicly.

186
00:12:57,611 --> 00:13:01,905
And there's no avoiding how tied
you and Doug are to Francis at this point.

187
00:13:01,906 --> 00:13:06,285
So, it's really just waiting
for the dust to settle. That's all.

188
00:13:07,161 --> 00:13:10,581
Why does it feel like you're telling me
my career is over, Madam Vice President?

189
00:13:10,582 --> 00:13:14,293
No, I'm just saying, you just need
to go away for a little while.

190
00:13:14,961 --> 00:13:18,714
And we'll bring you back into the fold
at a later date, and don't worry.

191
00:13:18,715 --> 00:13:21,634
Look at LeAnn.
She left and now she's back.

192
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:25,930
Have we ever had a drink together?

193
00:13:27,849 --> 00:13:29,016
Never.

194
00:13:47,243 --> 00:13:49,829
I wanted to hand this to you
while you were still president.

195
00:13:59,005 --> 00:14:01,340
I accept this with a heavy heart.

196
00:14:04,886 --> 00:14:07,138
I had a strategy session
with the attorneys yesterday.

197
00:14:07,764 --> 00:14:09,849
I hope they're treating you well.

198
00:14:13,144 --> 00:14:15,021
You know...

199
00:14:17,064 --> 00:14:20,610
Doug, we're not gonna be able
to see each other for some time now.

200
00:14:28,451 --> 00:14:30,537
So why don't you take something?

201
00:14:31,287 --> 00:14:33,288
- No.
- No, no. Go on. Take something.

202
00:14:33,289 --> 00:14:36,292
Anything. Anything you want.
Even if it's small.

203
00:14:37,669 --> 00:14:40,379
Something you can hold in your hand

204
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:45,217
to remind you of this place...
until you get back.

205
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:48,179
You go on.

206
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:57,749
We're a few hours away
from my official resignation...

207
00:15:58,500 --> 00:16:02,336
and you still have not agreed
to pardon me.

208
00:16:03,546 --> 00:16:05,130
And if you don't,

209
00:16:05,131 --> 00:16:09,217
I will be forced to renege
on that resignation.

210
00:16:09,218 --> 00:16:11,344
That would be outrageous.

211
00:16:11,345 --> 00:16:15,307
Well, it isn't official until I submit
a signed letter.

212
00:16:16,267 --> 00:16:18,519
And what would that do
to the rest of your presidency?

213
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:20,062
What would be left of it?

214
00:16:20,063 --> 00:16:23,691
Claire, if you don't do it, you're gonna
risk being married to a felon.

215
00:16:23,692 --> 00:16:26,318
And if I do, where does that leave me?

216
00:16:26,319 --> 00:16:29,029
Look, is this really the conversation
you want to be having?

217
00:16:29,030 --> 00:16:30,573
You've trapped me, Francis.

218
00:16:30,574 --> 00:16:33,283
No, I do not accept
that I've done something to you.

219
00:16:33,284 --> 00:16:37,329
I have provided you with an opportunity.

220
00:16:37,330 --> 00:16:41,750
Now, you have said before,
that this is your endgame.

221
00:16:41,751 --> 00:16:46,004
And now, your goal is
within spitting distance

222
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:50,051
and all you see is betrayal?
I don't buy it.

223
00:16:52,512 --> 00:16:55,306
Stop talking about what I've done to you.

224
00:16:58,893 --> 00:17:00,311
Admit it.

225
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:03,105
This is what you want.

226
00:17:04,148 --> 00:17:06,108
You were willing to kill for it.

227
00:17:07,484 --> 00:17:09,612
So, Claire, come and take it...

228
00:17:11,531 --> 00:17:13,365
before I take it back.

229
00:17:21,541 --> 00:17:25,044
We'll find the most strategic
time and place.

230
00:17:25,545 --> 00:17:27,421
But I will pardon you, Francis.

231
00:17:55,324 --> 00:17:57,826
For the good of the nation,
we need to disband this committee,

232
00:17:57,827 --> 00:17:59,536
and put this behind us.

233
00:17:59,537 --> 00:18:02,539
The president most likely
would not have survived the hearings.

234
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:05,668
You could argue that he had no choice
but to resign.

235
00:18:06,293 --> 00:18:08,837
But we can't deny that his testimony
struck a chord.

236
00:18:08,838 --> 00:18:10,798
Well, that may be true.

237
00:18:10,799 --> 00:18:13,341
But how is it that you,
Congressman Romero,

238
00:18:13,342 --> 00:18:16,804
his biggest critic,
are supporting him now?

239
00:18:19,473 --> 00:18:20,974
History.

240
00:18:20,975 --> 00:18:24,436
By the end of the day, the country
will have its first woman president.

241
00:18:25,146 --> 00:18:28,816
Look, I've always been a supporter
of the idea of a woman in the Oval Office.

242
00:18:28,817 --> 00:18:31,401
But when all is said and done,

243
00:18:31,402 --> 00:18:34,321
you do realize that Francis Underwood

244
00:18:34,322 --> 00:18:37,283
will still be sleeping
in the White House tonight?

245
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:55,050
Isn't this when you pack everything up?
Or at least take the personal things?

246
00:18:55,051 --> 00:18:56,886
I'm not taking anything.

247
00:18:59,305 --> 00:19:01,140
You can do what you want with it.

248
00:19:06,688 --> 00:19:09,691
- When do you meet with the US attorney?
- Day after tomorrow.

249
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:19,491
I never thought that Frank Underwood
would not be president.

250
00:19:20,451 --> 00:19:21,828
Not really.

251
00:19:26,165 --> 00:19:28,084
You could just run away.

252
00:19:29,585 --> 00:19:31,128
What does that get me?

253
00:19:31,713 --> 00:19:33,588
You're good at taking care of yourself.

254
00:19:35,591 --> 00:19:36,926
That's funny.

255
00:19:37,677 --> 00:19:39,845
Look, I want you to know
that I care for you,

256
00:19:39,846 --> 00:19:42,765
but I don't know how much I can be there.

257
00:19:49,521 --> 00:19:51,565
I think I'm gonna just sit here
for a while.

258
00:19:52,692 --> 00:19:54,318
Yeah, you should.

259
00:20:00,324 --> 00:20:02,659
Uh, the vice president would like you
to leave the White House

260
00:20:02,660 --> 00:20:03,870
before she's sworn in.

261
00:20:07,039 --> 00:20:09,624
She doesn't think it would be a good idea
for word to get out

262
00:20:09,625 --> 00:20:11,543
that you were here when it happened.

263
00:20:38,445 --> 00:20:41,656
<i>I do solemnly swear
that I will faithfully execute</i>

264
00:20:41,657 --> 00:20:45,118
<i>the office of President
of the United States,</i>

265
00:20:45,119 --> 00:20:47,412
<i>and will to the best of my ability</i>

266
00:20:47,413 --> 00:20:52,625
preserve, protect and defend
the Constitution of the United States.

267
00:20:52,626 --> 00:20:54,962
- So help me God.
- Here we are again.

268
00:20:54,963 --> 00:20:57,297
You know, if you ignore
all the pomp and circumstance,

269
00:20:57,298 --> 00:21:01,593
the most perverse thing is
I actually believe in the presidency.

270
00:21:01,594 --> 00:21:05,513
Its importance. What it means
around the world, even symbolically.

271
00:21:05,514 --> 00:21:10,477
But I believe in power even more.
For its own sake.

272
00:21:11,145 --> 00:21:15,565
Gore Vidal once wrote
that power is an end to itself,

273
00:21:15,566 --> 00:21:19,403
and the instinctive urge to prevail...

274
00:21:19,946 --> 00:21:22,824
the most important single human trait.

275
00:21:23,991 --> 00:21:27,452
I've always told myself that
everything I did was for her.

276
00:21:27,453 --> 00:21:31,916
But maybe it wasn't.
Maybe I love power more.

277
00:21:33,417 --> 00:21:36,669
<i>For you, and for any dear to you,</i>

278
00:21:36,670 --> 00:21:38,839
<i>I would do anything.</i>

279
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:41,549
<i>If my career were of that better kind</i>

280
00:21:41,550 --> 00:21:46,179
<i>that there was any opportunity
or capacity to sacrifice in it,</i>

281
00:21:46,180 --> 00:21:51,143
<i>I would embrace any sacrifice for you
and for those dear to you.</i>

282
00:21:51,811 --> 00:21:56,231
<i>Try to hold me in your mind,
at some quiet times,</i>

283
00:21:56,232 --> 00:22:00,235
<i>as ardent and sincere in this one thing.</i>

284
00:22:00,236 --> 00:22:01,945
<i>The time will come,</i>

285
00:22:01,946 --> 00:22:07,117
<i>the time will not be long in coming,
when new ties will be formed about you.</i>

286
00:22:07,118 --> 00:22:12,039
<i>The ties that will bind you
yet more tenderly and strongly</i>

287
00:22:12,040 --> 00:22:14,958
<i>to the home you so adorn.</i>

288
00:22:14,959 --> 00:22:19,046
<i>The dearest ties that will ever
grace and gladden you.</i>

289
00:22:19,047 --> 00:22:20,672
<i>Oh, Miss Manette,</i>

290
00:22:20,673 --> 00:22:25,052
<i>when the little picture of
a happy father's face looks up in yours...</i>

291
00:22:38,232 --> 00:22:40,234
Good evening.

292
00:22:41,860 --> 00:22:44,654
Good evening, ladies and gentlemen.
My name is Sean Jeffries.

293
00:22:44,655 --> 00:22:47,115
I'm the new deputy director
of communications.

294
00:22:47,116 --> 00:22:48,241
Where's Seth?

295
00:22:48,242 --> 00:22:52,162
Mr. Grayson got called away last minute,
so I'm temporarily filling his shoes.

296
00:22:52,163 --> 00:22:54,331
Uh, I...

297
00:22:54,332 --> 00:22:59,378
I won't be taking any questions. Instead,
I'll be reading from a prepared statement.

298
00:23:00,712 --> 00:23:02,089
A few hours ago,

299
00:23:02,090 --> 00:23:06,009
President Underwood resigned the office
of President of the United States.

300
00:23:06,010 --> 00:23:08,511
<i>And in a private ceremony
attended by staff,</i>

301
00:23:08,512 --> 00:23:11,639
<i>President Claire Underwood was sworn in.</i>

302
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:14,101
<i>Effective immediately,
she will be assuming the office</i>

303
00:23:14,102 --> 00:23:16,270
<i>of President of the United States.</i>

304
00:23:17,021 --> 00:23:20,191
<i>- Details will be coming shortly...</i>
- You must be so proud of him.

305
00:23:20,899 --> 00:23:23,485
<i>And while President Francis Underwood
couldn't be here today...</i>

306
00:23:23,486 --> 00:23:25,862
Transfer of power happened
three hours ago,

307
00:23:25,863 --> 00:23:28,740
quote, "privately and quietly."

308
00:23:28,741 --> 00:23:30,200
And that's above the fold.

309
00:23:30,201 --> 00:23:32,285
- Anything from DOJ?
- Nothing yet.

310
00:23:32,286 --> 00:23:33,578
No official title to him,

311
00:23:33,579 --> 00:23:35,622
but it's Mark Usher
running the transition.

312
00:23:35,623 --> 00:23:39,792
Okay.
Let's find out who's in and who's out.

313
00:23:39,793 --> 00:23:41,628
The dominoes are falling.

314
00:23:41,629 --> 00:23:43,547
- Now, who's on Romero?
- Here.

315
00:23:44,215 --> 00:23:47,092
- We want the congressman on the record.
- I've got it.

316
00:23:47,093 --> 00:23:49,636
And let's save Macallan for the weekend.

317
00:23:49,637 --> 00:23:51,973
Tom, where are we with Doug Stamper?

318
00:23:52,723 --> 00:23:54,682
There's, uh, something I need to check on.

319
00:23:54,683 --> 00:23:58,311
<i>Slugline,</i> BuzzFeed, half the outlets
in this city are ready to jump on this.

320
00:23:58,312 --> 00:24:00,397
You spoke to him. One on one.

321
00:24:00,398 --> 00:24:03,816
- He didn't actually say he did it.
- He doesn't have to.

322
00:24:03,817 --> 00:24:07,404
Does anyone know what Seth Grayson
said to the US attorney?

323
00:24:09,991 --> 00:24:11,200
Tom?

324
00:24:14,661 --> 00:24:17,497
Two years you've been writing
about this administration.

325
00:24:17,498 --> 00:24:20,084
- This is it.
- I want to follow up, that's all.

326
00:24:21,793 --> 00:24:24,129
<i>I see a beautiful city</i>

327
00:24:24,130 --> 00:24:27,174
<i>and a brilliant people rising
from this abyss.</i>

328
00:24:27,175 --> 00:24:30,760
<i>And in their struggles to be truly free,</i>

329
00:24:30,761 --> 00:24:33,138
<i>in their triumphs and defeats,</i>

330
00:24:33,139 --> 00:24:35,307
<i>through long years to come,</i>

331
00:24:35,308 --> 00:24:39,144
<i>I see the evil of this time
and of the previous time</i>

332
00:24:39,145 --> 00:24:42,189
<i>of which this is the natural birth,</i>

333
00:24:42,190 --> 00:24:47,111
<i>gradually making expiation for itself
and wearing out.</i>

334
00:24:48,612 --> 00:24:51,030
Surface-to-surface missiles
delivered sarin

335
00:24:51,031 --> 00:24:53,533
at about three o'clock in the morning,
our time.

336
00:24:53,534 --> 00:24:56,744
Moscow has already issued a statement
condemning the rebels

337
00:24:56,745 --> 00:24:59,497
for orchestrating
the attack on themselves.

338
00:24:59,498 --> 00:25:01,625
- And did they?
- Of course not.

339
00:25:02,251 --> 00:25:05,046
Petrov will use this
to justify air strikes.

340
00:25:05,921 --> 00:25:08,257
I'd like to show you an image.

341
00:25:15,347 --> 00:25:17,433
This one is coming out of Reuters.

342
00:25:18,059 --> 00:25:21,395
The feeling is most of the press
will be using it by the a.m.

343
00:25:22,271 --> 00:25:26,192
Experience tells me this will resonate
for about three to five days...

344
00:25:27,151 --> 00:25:28,651
which gives us our window.

345
00:25:28,652 --> 00:25:32,614
- Well, we can ready a statement.
- Troops on the ground is the statement.

346
00:25:32,615 --> 00:25:36,451
No, I don't want to do anything
until we find Ahmadi's location.

347
00:25:36,452 --> 00:25:39,078
I'm not sure we should wait on this,
Madam President.

348
00:25:39,079 --> 00:25:41,706
I'd like to remind you
that it was this administration

349
00:25:41,707 --> 00:25:43,500
that introduced the ultimatum.

350
00:25:43,501 --> 00:25:46,669
- You should act on it.
- Yes, but I barely have a team in place.

351
00:25:46,670 --> 00:25:48,630
Well, you can run it
by the former president...

352
00:25:48,631 --> 00:25:50,382
The former president is just that.

353
00:25:50,383 --> 00:25:54,636
- An opportunity has presented itself.
- And I'm trying to take advantage of it.

354
00:25:55,262 --> 00:25:58,515
- Is everyone in the Situation Room?
- As of 20 minutes ago.

355
00:26:08,275 --> 00:26:10,527
So, the timing is bad.

356
00:26:11,362 --> 00:26:13,863
If you pardon him now,
you're associated with his crimes.

357
00:26:13,864 --> 00:26:15,782
Republicans will have a field day.

358
00:26:16,367 --> 00:26:18,160
We need some cover.

359
00:26:18,161 --> 00:26:19,869
Well, that would be
Ahmadi's capture.

360
00:26:19,870 --> 00:26:23,122
- The right VP would help all this.
- Have you had any further thoughts?

361
00:26:23,123 --> 00:26:26,626
My short list is the same.
Westervelt, Clark, Klein.

362
00:26:26,627 --> 00:26:30,129
Klein would be the strongest bulwark
against calls for your impeachment.

363
00:26:30,130 --> 00:26:33,132
- Swallowing poison to stay alive.
- Alive is good.

364
00:26:33,133 --> 00:26:36,470
I don't think I can stomach Klein.
He called me a bitch. I prefer Clark.

365
00:26:37,346 --> 00:26:41,975
Tell me. Before you moved the body,
were you able to close his eyes?

366
00:26:43,310 --> 00:26:44,311
Yes.

367
00:26:47,231 --> 00:26:51,193
Look... I know his opinion
means a lot to you.

368
00:26:52,403 --> 00:26:53,736
Francis.

369
00:26:53,737 --> 00:26:56,573
But having him here, in the White House,
even in the East Wing,

370
00:26:56,574 --> 00:26:58,617
while we're trying to figure this out,
it's hard.

371
00:26:59,451 --> 00:27:02,996
At some point, someone is going to imply
that he is still making the decisions.

372
00:27:04,206 --> 00:27:05,624
That wouldn't be good.

373
00:27:11,004 --> 00:27:14,090
- I'll advise her. She'll come around.
- I hope so.

374
00:27:14,091 --> 00:27:17,760
Because if she doesn't act now,
when it comes to Syria,

375
00:27:17,761 --> 00:27:20,055
her presidency could be in danger.

376
00:27:20,889 --> 00:27:25,101
- And your future in doubt.
- Oh, don't threaten me, Ms. Davis.

377
00:27:25,102 --> 00:27:26,936
I don't threaten.

378
00:27:26,937 --> 00:27:29,606
I just try to remain as clear as possible.

379
00:27:29,607 --> 00:27:33,527
You offered me your services,
and I offered you mine.

380
00:27:35,362 --> 00:27:36,738
You know...

381
00:27:37,906 --> 00:27:41,034
I was here before you
and I'll be here after you.

382
00:27:41,952 --> 00:27:45,247
And regardless of that,
let me remind you...

383
00:27:45,248 --> 00:27:48,625
that nothing is more dangerous than me.

384
00:27:51,378 --> 00:27:54,964
You need to be practical now.
Davis isn't wrong.

385
00:27:54,965 --> 00:27:58,050
We've been trying to get our hands
on Ahmadi for a year, Francis.

386
00:27:58,051 --> 00:28:01,137
- She hasn't delivered.
- Yes, but this isn't about her.

387
00:28:01,138 --> 00:28:04,724
This is about you and coming out
with a strong message

388
00:28:04,725 --> 00:28:07,226
in your first address to the nation.

389
00:28:07,227 --> 00:28:10,814
This is about setting the course
for your presidency.

390
00:28:11,857 --> 00:28:13,400
Be strong, Claire.

391
00:28:14,360 --> 00:28:16,069
Go to war.

392
00:28:22,659 --> 00:28:24,328
But I need you to leave.

393
00:28:25,662 --> 00:28:27,205
Leave the White House.

394
00:28:30,251 --> 00:28:31,752
Yes, I see.

395
00:28:37,173 --> 00:28:41,428
For this pardon to succeed, Francis,
we need to appear to be estranged.

396
00:28:43,179 --> 00:28:45,224
I'm just being strategic.

397
00:28:46,475 --> 00:28:48,810
And where do you suggest I go?

398
00:28:49,395 --> 00:28:50,812
I'm not sure.

399
00:28:52,981 --> 00:28:55,149
The Naval Observatory?

400
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:58,152
Uh, I think the vice president's
residence is still too close.

401
00:28:58,153 --> 00:28:59,655
I'm sorry, I just...

402
00:29:00,572 --> 00:29:03,366
We can't have anyone think
you're still involved in policy.

403
00:29:03,367 --> 00:29:05,952
Look, if you're having second thoughts,
you should tell me now.

404
00:29:05,953 --> 00:29:08,162
- No. I'm in full agreement.
- 'Cause this is no time to hesitate.

405
00:29:08,163 --> 00:29:09,665
I am not hesitating.

406
00:29:10,499 --> 00:29:13,000
I just believe
if we don't play this correctly,

407
00:29:13,001 --> 00:29:14,544
as far as the public,

408
00:29:14,545 --> 00:29:18,465
my term will be nothing
but survival for both of us.

409
00:29:19,925 --> 00:29:21,176
All right.

410
00:29:23,136 --> 00:29:25,639
I want you to know I'm here if you need...

411
00:29:26,473 --> 00:29:31,978
any advice on policy or...
anything else you might need.

412
00:29:34,356 --> 00:29:36,983
Thank you. I'm going to bed.

413
00:29:44,658 --> 00:29:47,243
No one will ever love you as much as I do.

414
00:29:48,829 --> 00:29:50,121
I hope you know that.

415
00:29:51,748 --> 00:29:56,712
Just as I know that no one
will ever love me... like you.

416
00:31:56,122 --> 00:31:58,041
"Under the porcelain frog."

417
00:31:59,918 --> 00:32:03,672
The answers are case-sensitive and exact.
You won't get a second chance.

418
00:32:05,841 --> 00:32:08,802
- And the middle one?
- My favorite baseball player?

419
00:32:09,385 --> 00:32:11,638
"Wade Boggs." Two G's.

420
00:32:14,265 --> 00:32:18,687
And the last? "What did you leave
in that hotel room in Austin?"

421
00:32:21,356 --> 00:32:22,733
Where is my gun?

422
00:32:29,490 --> 00:32:30,782
Here you go.

423
00:32:39,458 --> 00:32:41,417
What guarantees do I have?

424
00:32:43,419 --> 00:32:45,005
I gave you your gun back.

425
00:32:48,634 --> 00:32:52,387
But what made you give it to him?
I'm curious.

426
00:32:53,472 --> 00:32:55,265
I thought he was in danger.

427
00:32:57,768 --> 00:32:59,603
And now you think what?

428
00:33:03,356 --> 00:33:05,567
That is what I'm asking.

429
00:33:07,611 --> 00:33:11,990
As long as I'm around,
you'll be a part of this administration.

430
00:33:12,783 --> 00:33:14,910
We both know too much about Aidan.

431
00:33:15,451 --> 00:33:18,705
And Claire knows how loyal you are.
I'm sure of it.

432
00:33:20,999 --> 00:33:25,587
So, what did you leave
in that hotel room in Austin?

433
00:33:30,341 --> 00:33:31,593
A bracelet.

434
00:33:32,719 --> 00:33:34,179
Oh, that's too bad.

435
00:33:39,350 --> 00:33:43,437
You know, I finally got a look at what
Macallan passed on to Ms. Harvey.

436
00:33:43,438 --> 00:33:45,607
I was shocked to realize the degree

437
00:33:45,608 --> 00:33:47,734
to which you and your husband
stole this election.

438
00:33:51,655 --> 00:33:54,782
I need to be honest with you.
I've been in talks with him about

439
00:33:54,783 --> 00:33:57,285
helping him start a foundation
of some kind.

440
00:33:57,911 --> 00:33:59,788
In exchange for influence over you.

441
00:34:03,416 --> 00:34:04,668
Interesting.

442
00:34:09,005 --> 00:34:11,800
I'm trying to help you
navigate this transition.

443
00:34:19,140 --> 00:34:20,601
Who are you to me?

444
00:34:23,103 --> 00:34:25,312
Who do you want me to be?

445
00:34:25,313 --> 00:34:26,940
That's not a good answer.

446
00:34:30,944 --> 00:34:34,947
You're the first woman President
of the United States.

447
00:34:34,948 --> 00:34:39,243
All you've had to swallow,
the sacrifices, the compromises.

448
00:34:39,244 --> 00:34:41,287
You're gonna want to isolate yourself.

449
00:34:41,913 --> 00:34:43,455
Not trust anyone.

450
00:34:43,456 --> 00:34:48,211
But that's exactly what you're gonna need.
Someone to tell you what's what.

451
00:34:49,545 --> 00:34:51,464
And is that person you?

452
00:34:55,927 --> 00:34:57,012
Is it?

453
00:34:57,596 --> 00:35:00,347
I don't think there's anything
I could say that would convince you

454
00:35:00,348 --> 00:35:01,683
if you don't already feel it.

455
00:35:03,852 --> 00:35:06,938
Ms. Davis,
you are asking me to start a war.

456
00:35:08,607 --> 00:35:12,026
And you seem to deliver on promises
when it suits you.

457
00:35:12,027 --> 00:35:14,738
So forgive me
if I question your intentions.

458
00:35:17,532 --> 00:35:18,784
I like you.

459
00:35:19,450 --> 00:35:20,994
I like being around you.

460
00:35:24,122 --> 00:35:27,375
And sometimes that makes me
less effective than I should be.

461
00:35:32,088 --> 00:35:37,093
Pardoning or not pardoning your husband,
in either case, he's a liability.

462
00:35:39,095 --> 00:35:41,222
If it's not treated properly...

463
00:35:42,265 --> 00:35:46,311
your husband's liver could fail him
at any time.

464
00:35:47,771 --> 00:35:49,981
It's not the kind of thing I could do.

465
00:35:51,191 --> 00:35:54,527
But I could find someone, or...

466
00:35:55,403 --> 00:36:00,532
I... I don't know if you realize, but...
even something like gelsemium

467
00:36:00,533 --> 00:36:04,079
can be lethal in higher doses.

468
00:36:08,750 --> 00:36:10,752
My husband's health is just fine.

469
00:36:13,922 --> 00:36:17,383
I'll continue to work with him.
Follow your lead.

470
00:36:21,722 --> 00:36:24,056
Here's my client's passport.

471
00:36:24,057 --> 00:36:27,184
- There's a few things we want to go over.
- That we haven't already?

472
00:36:27,185 --> 00:36:30,855
No cuffs, when you walk him out of here.
I need to be sure.

473
00:36:30,856 --> 00:36:33,734
Oh, come on, James,
we aren't gonna play that on this.

474
00:36:34,359 --> 00:36:37,236
You have some very good friends,
Mr. Stamper,

475
00:36:37,237 --> 00:36:39,072
to keep the press out of this.

476
00:36:39,865 --> 00:36:41,908
You will walk out of here
like a gentleman.

477
00:36:41,909 --> 00:36:44,952
We want him in front of the judge
within 12 hours.

478
00:36:44,953 --> 00:36:47,496
We don't even know
if we're gonna charge him yet.

479
00:36:47,497 --> 00:36:48,707
I did it.

480
00:36:49,624 --> 00:36:51,292
Let's get going.

481
00:36:55,255 --> 00:36:57,257
Who do you have on her cabinet?

482
00:36:58,174 --> 00:37:00,259
Right now, they're just suggestions.

483
00:37:00,260 --> 00:37:03,637
Oh, come on. We both know how this works.
You've already made your choices.

484
00:37:03,638 --> 00:37:05,348
You wouldn't be worth your salt
if you hadn't.

485
00:37:05,932 --> 00:37:08,226
I just want you to run them by me first.

486
00:37:08,935 --> 00:37:12,147
Look, I can make this transition
easy for you or not.

487
00:37:14,107 --> 00:37:16,108
And a word of advice.

488
00:37:16,109 --> 00:37:19,570
She's gonna need some friendly faces
looking at her across that table.

489
00:37:19,571 --> 00:37:20,613
There'll be a few...

490
00:37:21,572 --> 00:37:23,283
who will smile as required.

491
00:37:25,451 --> 00:37:26,828
Would you look at this?

492
00:37:30,999 --> 00:37:33,877
Both Special Forces. Former.

493
00:37:34,669 --> 00:37:37,296
They know how to forget,
so you don't have to worry about them.

494
00:37:39,632 --> 00:37:40,967
And the body?

495
00:37:43,344 --> 00:37:44,637
It's on ice.

496
00:37:48,308 --> 00:37:51,310
I just made contact with Nasser.

497
00:37:51,311 --> 00:37:54,105
We have secured the location of Ahmadi.

498
00:37:54,689 --> 00:37:57,316
- I'll assemble the team.
- I called Admiral Dale already.

499
00:37:57,317 --> 00:37:58,901
So we have some decisions to make.

500
00:37:58,902 --> 00:38:02,113
Once we have troops on the ground,
we'll need to take a close look

501
00:38:02,114 --> 00:38:04,240
at who we're considering for your cabinet.

502
00:38:04,241 --> 00:38:06,117
You'll need a team around you
with wartime experience.

503
00:38:06,118 --> 00:38:08,577
I have some suggestions
I've passed on to Mark.

504
00:38:08,578 --> 00:38:12,039
I think Deputy Director of the CIA,
Marcy Siegerson,

505
00:38:12,040 --> 00:38:16,418
would make a terrific Secretary of State.
Someone I could easily liaison with.

506
00:38:16,419 --> 00:38:20,547
Well, I was hoping that you would be
on my cabinet, in some capacity.

507
00:38:20,548 --> 00:38:24,093
I'll be operating out of the region.
It's where my strength lies.

508
00:38:24,094 --> 00:38:26,262
There are better people
who can take it from here,

509
00:38:26,263 --> 00:38:27,972
advise you on the home front.

510
00:38:27,973 --> 00:38:31,934
And Ms. Harvey, LeAnn,
we need to move you.

511
00:38:31,935 --> 00:38:34,020
Uh, just for now, of course.

512
00:38:34,021 --> 00:38:37,231
- It was my understanding that...
- Right now a more seasoned Chief of Staff

513
00:38:37,232 --> 00:38:40,443
would send a strong message to
the Congress and to the nation. For now.

514
00:39:01,172 --> 00:39:03,299
She'll do it. She'll send in the troops.

515
00:39:03,300 --> 00:39:05,343
I'll be in Dubai by tomorrow afternoon.

516
00:39:06,302 --> 00:39:08,012
And our deal stays in place.

517
00:39:08,013 --> 00:39:10,014
Yeah, hold on a second.

518
00:39:10,015 --> 00:39:11,266
- Ready?
- Go ahead.

519
00:39:16,604 --> 00:39:20,149
Yes. Ms. Harvey has her gun back.

520
00:39:20,150 --> 00:39:23,235
Macallan's files are with the president.

521
00:39:23,236 --> 00:39:26,864
Any hard evidence connecting you
to the election...

522
00:39:26,865 --> 00:39:28,491
<i>is in her hands.</i>

523
00:39:29,284 --> 00:39:31,411
Then LeAnn's job is done.

524
00:40:19,125 --> 00:40:21,877
If you have anything to say,
now is the time.

525
00:40:25,966 --> 00:40:27,633
What do you think happened?

526
00:40:29,677 --> 00:40:31,428
I'd prefer you tell me that.

527
00:40:31,429 --> 00:40:34,474
Humor me. You asked for this meeting.

528
00:40:35,641 --> 00:40:37,268
What do you think happened?

529
00:40:42,315 --> 00:40:44,025
I believe Zoe Barnes was investigating

530
00:40:44,026 --> 00:40:46,402
a relationship you were having
with Rachel Posner.

531
00:40:47,237 --> 00:40:50,072
And somehow, that knowledge would endanger

532
00:40:50,073 --> 00:40:54,535
Francis Underwood,
who you would do anything for.

533
00:40:56,496 --> 00:40:59,124
But did anyone think
about the life of Zoe Barnes?

534
00:41:02,460 --> 00:41:04,963
You know,
you think you can erase something.

535
00:41:06,381 --> 00:41:08,799
Then you find out that's not possible.

536
00:41:10,593 --> 00:41:14,222
Tom, my attorneys didn't even want me
to speak with you.

537
00:41:15,056 --> 00:41:17,724
I'm sorry,
there's just nothing more to say here.

538
00:41:17,725 --> 00:41:20,061
I don't know what happened
to Rachel Posner.

539
00:41:20,853 --> 00:41:23,523
But I don't believe you killed Zoe Barnes.

540
00:41:24,774 --> 00:41:27,110
Is this you in this video?

541
00:41:32,823 --> 00:41:34,325
Looks like me.

542
00:41:47,672 --> 00:41:50,675
I've thought long and hard, Francis.

543
00:41:51,551 --> 00:41:53,094
Barely slept.

544
00:41:53,969 --> 00:41:55,471
That's the job.

545
00:41:57,140 --> 00:42:00,476
I'm going to send in troops.
I'll be announcing it tomorrow night.

546
00:42:02,020 --> 00:42:04,064
I think you're doing the right thing.

547
00:42:07,067 --> 00:42:08,318
Do you hate it here?

548
00:42:09,069 --> 00:42:11,112
Oh, you know I don't like hotels.

549
00:42:12,238 --> 00:42:15,825
An approximation of home
just to remind you you're not there.

550
00:42:18,869 --> 00:42:20,705
Well, we don't live in a home.

551
00:42:21,872 --> 00:42:24,792
We live in a house,
borrowed and temporary.

552
00:42:28,671 --> 00:42:31,591
Something in your eye. A look.

553
00:42:32,425 --> 00:42:33,801
It's changed.

554
00:42:36,762 --> 00:42:39,057
We're the same now, you and I.

555
00:42:39,890 --> 00:42:42,017
- How so?
- You know how.

556
00:42:43,269 --> 00:42:45,771
It's been a long time
since I surprised myself.

557
00:42:48,483 --> 00:42:50,025
You'll recover.

558
00:42:51,319 --> 00:42:54,363
You're the most powerful woman
in the world, Claire.

559
00:42:54,364 --> 00:42:56,866
Comfort pales by comparison.

560
00:43:00,495 --> 00:43:03,830
I'll announce it during the speech,
after the troops.

561
00:43:03,831 --> 00:43:06,167
A full and unconditional pardon...

562
00:43:07,293 --> 00:43:10,212
for Francis Underwood and any crimes
he might have committed

563
00:43:10,213 --> 00:43:12,757
against the United States while president.

564
00:43:14,342 --> 00:43:15,926
I'm glad to hear that.

565
00:43:16,677 --> 00:43:20,806
It was never in doubt.
I just needed to think about how.

566
00:43:23,893 --> 00:43:26,687
So how long does this arrangement last?

567
00:43:26,688 --> 00:43:27,855
For the time being.

568
00:43:31,066 --> 00:43:33,527
How did we get here, Francis?

569
00:43:33,528 --> 00:43:35,863
Oh, let it go. It's done.

570
00:43:38,366 --> 00:43:39,992
Oh, and one word of advice.

571
00:43:40,701 --> 00:43:43,162
Whomever Usher offers up to you
as vice president,

572
00:43:43,163 --> 00:43:46,124
that's the person
that you're really gonna have to watch.

573
00:43:47,708 --> 00:43:50,503
I won't choose anyone I can't manage.

574
00:44:35,256 --> 00:44:37,466
<i>Southwest corner
of the building. Maintain visual.</i>

575
00:44:37,467 --> 00:44:38,551
<i>Copy that.</i>

576
00:44:39,302 --> 00:44:41,346
<i>Frag out!</i>

577
00:44:43,431 --> 00:44:45,266
<i>There's Ahmadi.
I have visual on Ahmadi.</i>

578
00:44:45,267 --> 00:44:47,434
<i>- I see him.
- Go, go! Fire!</i>

579
00:44:53,983 --> 00:44:55,776
I made a terrible mistake.

580
00:44:59,071 --> 00:45:00,823
What did you do?

581
00:45:01,782 --> 00:45:04,535
I don't even know what I'm doing here.
I, uh...

582
00:45:05,411 --> 00:45:08,581
This morning I started driving.
I... I got scared.

583
00:45:10,833 --> 00:45:13,585
Anyway, I'm on my way back.
Can I come see you?

584
00:45:13,586 --> 00:45:14,920
Yes, please.

585
00:45:53,376 --> 00:45:57,297
Sometimes you don't have to watch
the whole movie to know how it ends.

586
00:46:02,176 --> 00:46:04,595
The speech is gonna play well
with both parties.

587
00:46:05,888 --> 00:46:07,639
Where are we with the Republicans?

588
00:46:07,640 --> 00:46:09,642
Trading names
when it comes to your cabinet.

589
00:46:10,310 --> 00:46:12,394
We have our generals, which is good.

590
00:46:12,395 --> 00:46:16,440
Some corporate types, outsiders.
Make you seem like a renegade.

591
00:46:16,441 --> 00:46:17,942
Corporate, from where?

592
00:46:18,984 --> 00:46:21,987
Oil, banking, mostly. Some tech.

593
00:46:22,613 --> 00:46:24,865
Occasional D.C. lifer sprinkled
into the mix

594
00:46:24,866 --> 00:46:26,742
to make sure the trains run on time.

595
00:46:26,743 --> 00:46:28,827
I was going over our list
for vice president.

596
00:46:28,828 --> 00:46:30,162
Yeah. Hold on.

597
00:46:30,830 --> 00:46:33,874
Uh, this will seem unexpected,

598
00:46:33,875 --> 00:46:37,712
but a lot of the people
I spoke to suggested me.

599
00:46:42,675 --> 00:46:44,677
You're not a politician.

600
00:46:45,720 --> 00:46:47,345
Exactly.

601
00:46:47,346 --> 00:46:49,431
But I could be by your side.

602
00:46:49,432 --> 00:46:52,935
Most of the Hill and the Senate
would not come near us.

603
00:46:55,145 --> 00:46:58,608
- I'll take it into consideration.
- It's beyond that. You'll need me.

604
00:46:59,692 --> 00:47:01,026
Excuse me?

605
00:47:01,819 --> 00:47:03,654
I can help. Look...

606
00:47:04,655 --> 00:47:07,742
It is the way
to keep you in power.

607
00:47:09,369 --> 00:47:11,161
And keep your secrets.

608
00:47:22,382 --> 00:47:23,549
Good evening.

609
00:47:24,133 --> 00:47:28,094
I'm here to report to the American people
and the world

610
00:47:28,095 --> 00:47:33,851
that early this morning, Special Forces
killed the ICO terrorist Ahmed Al Ahmadi.

611
00:47:34,519 --> 00:47:35,811
We got him.

612
00:47:36,937 --> 00:47:38,188
We got him.

613
00:47:39,148 --> 00:47:41,983
Now, there comes a time
in every president's tenure

614
00:47:41,984 --> 00:47:46,112
when he or she must face the question
of whether or not

615
00:47:46,113 --> 00:47:49,450
to send young American soldiers
into harm's way.

616
00:47:50,325 --> 00:47:51,619
In my case...

617
00:47:52,244 --> 00:47:56,624
that time has fallen within
the very first days of my presidency.

618
00:47:57,875 --> 00:48:01,670
<i>Russian President Viktor Petrov
collaborated with the Chinese</i>

619
00:48:01,671 --> 00:48:04,965
<i>on illegal oil exploration in Antarctica.</i>

620
00:48:04,966 --> 00:48:08,218
<i>Recently, we have learned
that he has sent troops</i>

621
00:48:08,219 --> 00:48:10,471
<i>to fight alongside the Syrian regime,</i>

622
00:48:10,472 --> 00:48:13,765
<i>assisting them in the destruction
of the Syrian nation.</i>

623
00:48:13,766 --> 00:48:17,811
These forces are using chemical weapons
on their own people,

624
00:48:17,812 --> 00:48:22,483
torturing the opposition, and starving
huge segments of the population.

625
00:48:22,484 --> 00:48:24,735
The Syrians are a people besieged.

626
00:48:25,319 --> 00:48:28,446
Let them not also be forgotten.

627
00:48:28,447 --> 00:48:32,868
The time has come for our outrage
to be turned into action.

628
00:48:33,786 --> 00:48:37,372
Five months ago, my husband addressed
the House of Representatives

629
00:48:37,373 --> 00:48:40,751
and asked them to declare war on ICO.

630
00:48:40,752 --> 00:48:42,545
Congress failed him.

631
00:48:43,629 --> 00:48:45,506
Congress failed you.

632
00:48:46,466 --> 00:48:52,597
ICO extremists want democracy
and America itself to die a fiery death.

633
00:48:53,514 --> 00:48:56,141
We cannot allow that to happen.

634
00:48:56,142 --> 00:49:00,730
We can't wait for Congress any longer.
We gave Congress every chance.

635
00:49:01,522 --> 00:49:03,023
She isn't going to say it.

636
00:49:04,233 --> 00:49:07,611
Now, history judges every leader,
every president,

637
00:49:07,612 --> 00:49:10,906
by how he or she treats
his or her own people.

638
00:49:10,907 --> 00:49:15,952
A regime that would target hospitals,
refugee camps,

639
00:49:15,953 --> 00:49:21,458
schools or bread lines in order
to retain power must be confronted.

640
00:49:21,459 --> 00:49:26,964
A leader that would sacrifice the physical
and emotional well-being of his citizens,

641
00:49:27,798 --> 00:49:30,216
<i>that would treat his people as pawns,</i>

642
00:49:30,217 --> 00:49:33,595
just to stay in power? Well...

643
00:49:33,596 --> 00:49:36,724
that leader needs to be stopped.

644
00:49:39,644 --> 00:49:41,812
If she doesn't pardon me...

645
00:49:43,272 --> 00:49:44,524
I'll kill her.

646
00:49:46,191 --> 00:49:49,695
Thank you
and God bless this great country.

647
00:49:57,161 --> 00:49:59,537
Well, the calls are coming in already.

648
00:49:59,538 --> 00:50:01,623
Well done.
This'll be a good night for you.

649
00:50:01,624 --> 00:50:02,749
Nothing from Moscow yet.

650
00:50:02,750 --> 00:50:04,877
Right now I just need some time to myself.

651
00:50:10,507 --> 00:50:12,467
Do you know Tom Yates?

652
00:50:12,468 --> 00:50:14,385
Uh, not personally. Why?

653
00:50:14,386 --> 00:50:16,305
He hasn't been around in a while.

654
00:50:17,222 --> 00:50:18,766
I don't know, forget it.

655
00:50:19,684 --> 00:50:20,726
What?

656
00:50:20,727 --> 00:50:24,354
I've been calling him.
And he usually answers.

657
00:50:25,773 --> 00:50:28,358
We demand justice,
we demand peace!

658
00:50:28,359 --> 00:50:30,694
No more war in the Middle East!

659
00:50:30,695 --> 00:50:33,321
We demand justice, we demand peace!

660
00:50:33,322 --> 00:50:35,741
No more war in the Middle East!

661
00:50:35,742 --> 00:50:38,368
We demand justice, we demand peace!

662
00:50:38,369 --> 00:50:40,787
No more war in the Middle East!

663
00:50:40,788 --> 00:50:44,082
We demand justice, we demand peace...

664
00:50:44,083 --> 00:50:46,459
<i>The anti-war demonstrations
outside the White House</i>

665
00:50:46,460 --> 00:50:47,628
<i>finally got out of hand.</i>

666
00:50:47,629 --> 00:50:50,421
<i>You've reached
LeAnn Harvey. Please leave a message.</i>

667
00:50:50,422 --> 00:50:52,841
<i>One of the protesters
made his way over the gates.</i>

668
00:50:52,842 --> 00:50:54,885
<i>As he was running across
the White House lawn,</i>

669
00:50:54,886 --> 00:50:59,014
<i>Secret Service agents moved in,
tragically shooting and killing the man.</i>

670
00:51:07,106 --> 00:51:09,858
<i>You've reached
LeAnn Harvey. Please leave a message.</i>

671
00:51:09,859 --> 00:51:11,694
Hey, where are you?

672
00:51:45,895 --> 00:51:48,521
I'm sorry, ma'am,
it's just not possible tonight.

673
00:51:48,522 --> 00:51:49,815
We can't secure the run.

674
00:51:49,816 --> 00:51:52,276
The level of threat at this point
is just too high.

675
00:51:53,110 --> 00:51:55,487
- Okay. Thank you.
- Yes, ma'am.

676
00:53:19,613 --> 00:53:21,031
My turn.

677
00:53:21,032 --> 00:53:25,032
<b><font color="#ff0000">Sync and corrections by btsix
www.addic7ed.com</font></b>

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
